WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
Tanukichi

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
Diner

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:08.040
Be delicious. Be delicious. Be delicious.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.160
Okay, Dad, I'll be back later!

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.710
Okay. Cheer him on for all of us, okay?

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.230
Today's the individual competition, huh?

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:17.780
Yeah!

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.600
This time, he'll get first!

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.080
Yeah!

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:21.950
Give it your best!

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.840
There are forty entrants in
today's individual competition.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:29.260
Well, there were no qualifying rounds,

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.170
but still, having this many entrants
to a new tournament is impressive.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:37.020
And the set piece is
"Jongara-bushi: Shinkyuubushi."

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:41.560
There's a lot of freedom in that piece.
They can showcase their creativity.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.220
It's a seriously hard piece to play, though.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:49.680
The decisive factor will be how much
of their own sound they can show.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.950
Is that...

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.950
Kamiki Ryuugen?!

00:00:57.580 --> 00:00:59.690
Whoa, that's a shock!

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:01.760
What's Tanuma's dad doing in a place like this?

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.950
He doesn't even show up
to the Aomori tournaments.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.460
Well, this is a strange turn of events.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:17.970
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:24.560
<i>Why's this guy sitting next to me?</i>

00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:30.290
<i>The individual competition will now begin.</i>

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:53.500
Those Snow White Notes

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.950
Episode 10
Wind From the
Mountains

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.950
<i>From Senshinkan High School of
Yamagata Prefecture: Nakai Yuuki-kun.</i>

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:13.460
Want some?

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:15.840
Huh?

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.240
No.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:18.960
It's...

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:20.960
...battle food.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.840
"Battle food"?

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:27.620
On the day of a competition and
the day before it, I eat red things.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.870
Today, it's red bean rice.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.320
And you know something?

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.770
The red bean rice from around here isn't sweet.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:43.210
Sawamura! So this is where you've been!

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:44.670
Seriously, you!

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.900
You haven't signed in at reception, right?

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.110
They'll consider you a no-show if you don't.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:51.940
And our master teacher
Oodawara is totally freaking out.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.040
I'm totally freaking out!

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:54.590
See?

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.580
Wh-What is it?

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.240
You know something?

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:03.610
The red bean rice in Tokyo is flavorless.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.200
What are you talking about?!

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.310
Just season it with toasted sesame salt!

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.430
What was all that about?

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:13.880
The sekihan in Aomori has
sugar in it, so it's sweet.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.060
Really?

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:23.510
<i>My friend... has left.</i>

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.610
<i>And yet...</i>

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.410
<i>I cannot go.</i>

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:32.480
<i>Once I start eating, I must
finish my meal where I'm sitting.</i>

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:35.290
<i>And then...</i>

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:37.960
<i>I must take this pebble...</i>

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.550
<i>and kick it all the way to the venue entrance!</i>

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.120
<i>As I suspected, the lack of any
qualifying rounds has made this a chore.</i>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.650
Tachikawa
Sho

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.650
Arakawa

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.650
Sawatari

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.650
Kataoka

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:58.650
<i>Hurry it up.</i>

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:03.360
<i>I want to listen to the children who have
already duked it out at the national level.</i>

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:08.370
<i>The ones to watch in the morning
group are Arakawa Ushio, and...</i>

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:12.910
<i>the boy who was on the winning team in
yesterday's group competition, Kaji Takaomi.</i>

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:15.560
<i>The highlight of the afternoon group</i>

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.880
<i>will undoubtedly be Kamiki
Ryuugen's son, Tanuma Souichi.</i>

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:20.210
<i>And...</i>

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.000
Tanuma

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.130
Shimizu

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.130
Yamazaki

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:22.170
Endou

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:23.170
<i>Even though this is the first time
I've seen or heard his name,</i>

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.370
<i>I can't help wondering about </i>this<i> boy.</i>

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.050
Sawamura-kun, it says
you're Contestant Number 36.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:33.310
Competitors with proven skills
usually get put near the end.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.020
Really? Then, isn't this a bit strange?

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.060
Sawamura-kun hasn't taken
part in a tournament before.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.160
<i>It must be Umeko's doing.</i>

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:52.920
K-Kamiki Ryuugen?!

00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:59.160
His ailing master teacher gave him a massive,
<i>exceptional</i> promotion in his early forties!

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:04.170
Since then, he's reigned over the Kamiki
SchoolвЂ”No, the entire shamisen world!

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.760
He's a very important person!

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:08.390
So you're finally playing for people?

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:10.310
Huh? Do you two know each other?

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:11.800
Oh me, oh my...

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:18.480
What brings you all the way from Aomori?

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:21.980
I came to ascertain my son's abilities.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.320
Souichi's abilities? But why now?

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:27.470
You hardly ever turn up
to competitions back home.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:36.300
Souichi's abilities are the real deal.
I do not need to confirm them.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:40.250
To tell you the truth... I've come here...

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.550
...to ascertain Setsu's abilities.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.860
<i>Son?</i>

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:48.170
<i>Souichi? Setsu?</i>

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:49.340
What's going on?

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:52.270
Is this a sudden scandal?

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.480
You really are a self-centered old man.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.020
Hello?

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:09.730
Huh?

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:15.620
I saw him on the monitors.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.280
Bring that moron here!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.840
Allow us to escort you.

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:25.840
Her orders.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:28.410
Kouta, keep an eye on Setsu for me.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.430
Oh, uh, sure.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.100
I'm looking forward to it.

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:40.770
Though you're unlikely to
beat Souichi as you are now.

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:50.190
Sawamura-kun...

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.430
It's hard to know what to say to him.

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:55.120
At a time like this, it's best
to just leave him alone.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:07:59.480
Setsu.

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:02.410
You okay?

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.510
Do I look like I'm not?

00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:06.840
Hm, well, you <i>look</i> like you're okay...

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.290
Don't ask, then.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:10.460
It's normal to ask, right?

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:13.360
After all, Wakana-chan asked
me to keep an eye on you.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:16.220
And I really don't like Tanuma's dad.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.730
U-Um...

00:08:18.730 --> 00:08:22.900
About that man earlier who
said he was Sawamura's father...

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:19.720
Ba-dump

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:26.730
D-Does that make Mai and Sawamura... siblings?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.070
Seriously, this girl
What <i>are</i> you asking him?!

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.670
That's an invasion of privacy!

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.290
So I shouldn't ask?

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.470
They're not siblings.
Souichi and Mai are adopted.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:38.290
The only one related to
that guy by blood is Setsu.

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.920
Kouta.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:44.180
It's common knowledge out in the country.
Hiding it will only cause issues down the line.

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:48.040
<i>This guy with the natural curls is spilling
dirty little secrets like they're nothing!</i>

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.200
<i>Can't he read the mood?
Or is this actually refreshing?</i>

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:53.300
<i>So wait, Sawamura and Maimai
can still get married, right?</i>

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.130
Tanuma's dad is a loyal
devotee of Setsu's Gramps.

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:00.440
Go die.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.440
I can't concentrate here.

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.010
Oh, uh...

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.020
I made a lunch for you.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:15.270
My dad and everyone in the
shopping district is rooting for you.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:16.240
Thank you.

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.740
S-Sawamura-kun, you can do it.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:24.760
You can do it!

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:27.740
We're rooting for you!

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:33.850
Um... What's Sawamura-kun usually like?

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:35.920
Like that.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.840
What's Setsu-san like at school?

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:43.100
He usually sleeps through class.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:45.570
<i>This girl...</i>

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:47.320
<i>This person...</i>

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.570
<i>...is so cute!</i>

00:09:48.920 --> 00:09:50.090
I see.

00:09:50.090 --> 00:09:53.440
<i>So he even lets his pheromones
loose on young girls like her, huh?</i>

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:56.030
<i>Sawamura, you're a man to be feared!</i>

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.040
Entrants'
Waiting Room

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:07.420
Your stubbornness is exasperating.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:12.250
Same goes for your insensitivity,
seeking out Setsu while your wife is here.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:15.050
She understands me and how I think.

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:18.840
She might know how you feel,
but that's not the same as understanding.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.060
I've already told you
I won't let you have Setsu.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:24.030
Why do you need to gauge his abilities?

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.720
I've been thinking...

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:35.710
I know it's difficult to hear,
but I can't hold back my feelings.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:40.990
I want Setsu to inherit the title
of Kamiki Ryuugen from me.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.870
Your school doesn't do
hereditary succession.

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:47.370
Choose one of your talented disciples.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.620
Besides, he doesn't play in the Kamiki style.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:53.640
That's why I keep telling
you I want to take him in!

00:10:54.030 --> 00:10:55.880
<i>This man...</i>

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.460
What I want is Matsugorou.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.390
As long as I have his sound, that's enough.

00:11:01.690 --> 00:11:03.390
<i>...is a demon of the arts.</i>

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:07.150
Matsugorou's sound belongs
to me, his daughter.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:09.260
I'm not giving Setsu to you.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:11.780
<i>This one's a demon, too.</i>

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.780
It's mine. I'm not letting
anyone else have it.

00:11:16.270 --> 00:11:18.580
<i>And it's not just these two.</i>

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.440
<i>Mai's fixation with Setsu...</i>

00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:27.480
<i>And the way Souichi doesn't
pay any mind to anyone.</i>

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.790
I have arrived.

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:34.610
Souichi.

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.630
Do your best out there.

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:43.720
<i>Dad didn't come yesterday, but now...</i>

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.310
You're an idiot.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:46.480
Huh?

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:49.550
Setsu needs to learn other sounds.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:53.280
This tournament will end with him
getting obliterated by Souichi.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.670
This conversation is over.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:01.990
Setsu will win.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:03.740
And if you say anything like that again...

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:06.120
I'll kill you.

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:09.120
<i>Everyone...</i>

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:11.770
<i>...is so exhausting to be around.</i>

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.070
Oh, is this...

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:43.200
Hey, Kaji!

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:49.370
I got beat in the group competition,
but I won't lose in the individuals.

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:52.760
You're pretty much the
only one who'd talk to anyone

00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:55.040
in this tense atmosphere.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:57.920
That's because they're all weak.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:01.430
Contestant Number 21, Arakawa Ushio-kun?

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.010
That's me.

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:03.440
Later.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:05.740
Later.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.980
<i>Contestant Number 19.</i>

00:13:07.980 --> 00:13:11.630
<i>From Minami Aoki High School of
Fukushima Prefecture: Tanaka Ichirou-kun.</i>

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:09.660
Hey.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:11.530
<i>They're ignoring me?</i>

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:13.290
<i>How petty can you get?!</i>

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:15.610
Listen up, Arakawa!

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:17.230
Use the Twang sparingly!

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:18.650
Do <i>not </i>overuse the Twang!

00:13:21.070 --> 00:13:22.240
Forget that.

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:31.140
E-Excuse me...

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.280
Allow me to show you to your seat.

00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:35.810
Please, don't trouble yourself.

00:13:41.870 --> 00:13:43.340
<i>Just a little longer.</i>

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:01.740
<i>A little longer.</i>

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:09.620
<i>All righty.</i>

00:14:10.310 --> 00:14:11.620
<i>Contestant Number 21.</i>

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:15.890
<i>From Touhou Academy of
Fukushima Prefecture: Arakawa Ushio-kun.</i>

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:17.620
Right here!

00:14:17.620 --> 00:14:19.290
Ushio!

00:14:18.920 --> 00:14:20.750
Arakawa
Ushio

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:20.750
Go for it!

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:24.610
So it's okay to cheer loudly in
shamisen tournaments, huh?

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:27.510
It is, but this guy's something else.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:30.010
Oh! It's the guy who did
all that intense sliding.

00:14:30.280 --> 00:14:31.360
What?

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:33.800
He was a hoot in the group competition.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:36.690
Oh, the guy who did all that
crazy grandstanding, right?

00:14:36.690 --> 00:14:39.100
Well, let's see how he does in the individuals.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:47.150
<i>Now, then...</i>

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:53.410
<i>Let's liven things up!</i>

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:04.440
He's doing the Twang right off the bat!

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:06.590
Use it <i>sparingly</i>! I'm begging you!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:09.130
<i>Sparingly? Are you stupid?</i>

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.760
<i>My motto is: "Enjoy yourself"!</i>

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.480
That was so cool just now!

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:14.840
Do it again!

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:21.020
<i>Striking the strings is so much fun,
he just can't help himself, huh?</i>

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:23.130
<i>His posture's terrible.</i>

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:24.920
<i>He's the complete opposite of me.</i>

00:15:26.030 --> 00:15:30.080
<i>I have weapons of my own, but even so...</i>

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:33.600
<i>Sometimes, I just get so frustrated.</i>

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.040
<i>He's not up for a while yet.</i>

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:42.090
<i>Isn't he worried other people's
performances will stick in his head?</i>

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:46.420
<i>Small, fine, brisk...</i>

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.630
<i>And then!</i>

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:49.050
Ah! Here it comes!

00:15:51.020 --> 00:15:52.100
There it is!

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:53.130
I shouldn't laugh!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.350
Don't overuse the Twang!
It'll leave a worse impression!

00:15:58.350 --> 00:16:00.850
Huh? Wait, is he...

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:02.920
Is he smiling?

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.950
Okay, fine. As it's come to this...

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:14.070
Arakawa, go for it!

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:18.330
It looks so fun!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:21.370
So it's okay to move around that much, huh?

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:25.040
Not really. If a teacher was up
there with him, he'd get scolded.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:35.120
<i>The buzz of a slide is so different
from the sound of a strike.</i>

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:37.390
<i>It's obnoxious?</i>

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.390
<i>Go ahead! Say what you want!</i>

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.700
<i>I wanted to hear that buzz so much,</i>

00:16:42.700 --> 00:16:46.100
<i>I slid up and down the strings
day after day like an idiot.</i>

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:48.970
<i>I want to enjoy myself!</i>

00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:57.200
<i>Oh, man...</i>

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.370
<i>This feels so good!</i>

00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:02.700
He's doing it too much.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:05.610
Though, with all the
repeated sliding he's doing,

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:09.300
the fact he doesn't miss his
fingering on the return is amazing.

00:17:09.530 --> 00:17:12.510
And more than anything,
you can tell he's having fun.

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.220
<i>And now, I'll close it out
with my Arakawa Twang!</i>

00:17:45.680 --> 00:17:49.520
Dang it, Arakawa! That was <i>insanely</i> fun!

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:52.460
Maybe you just always need to
play that way! That was great!

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.400
That was amazing!

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:56.720
Seems individual rounds
are where he really shines.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:17:58.730
He stands out <i>way</i> too much!

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:01.720
The judges will probably
be split on this one.

00:18:02.790 --> 00:18:04.880
Yeah! Peace!

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:10.960
<i>All right!</i>

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:14.010
<i>My performance was a
ten out of ten!</i>

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.550
<i>Now, then...</i>

00:18:17.550 --> 00:18:21.950
<i>How many more will be able to give
a performance as amazing as that?</i>

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:25.210
<i>Being able to hold his ground and be himself...</i>

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:28.460
<i>To excite the crowd like that...
There's no way I can match him.</i>

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:31.370
<i>Next up, Contestant Number 22.</i>

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:35.090
<i>From Minamida Technical High School
of Akita Prefecture...</i>

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:38.840
You're unlikely to beat
Souichi as you are now.

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:42.140
<i>What is a "winning sound"?</i>

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:49.840
Contestant Number 29, Kaji Takaomi-kun?

00:18:49.840 --> 00:18:50.760
Oh, yes.

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.120
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:03.500
<i>I feel like my heart's gonna
jump out of my mouth!</i>

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:07.620
Kaji-kun, you're really good, but...

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:10.170
Tsugaru\h\hShamisen\h\hClasses

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:10.170
Folk songs\h\h\h\hShamisen
Traditional Drums\h\h\h\h\hBeginners

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.160
Your sound's too gentle.

00:19:10.520 --> 00:19:13.510
You need to strike harder
and put more emotion into it.

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:17.870
When you play solo, you never manage to
show more than half your usual ability.

00:19:17.870 --> 00:19:20.320
You have to keep your nerves in check.

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:24.010
You're right, but I can't fix
what can't be fixed.

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:26.940
I know, I'll show you something amazing.

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:32.830
This is from the Hirosaki Tournament
in May. I was utterly defeated.

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:35.950
That's the A-level runner up, Tanuma Souichi.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:38.950
I've heard that name a lot.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:41.640
Considering my age, I'll never beat him.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:44.500
On one hand, he's amazing.
On the other, it frustrates me.

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:49.680
Kaji-kun, you should use this
feeling as your driving force.

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:51.750
No, you <i>must</i> use it like that.

00:19:52.810 --> 00:19:54.170
<i>Contestant Number 29.</i>

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:58.120
<i>From Yamazan High School of
Osaka Prefecture: Kaji Takaomi-kun.</i>

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.470
<i>That's a lot of cheering.</i>

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.890
<i>There's the little puppy.</i>

00:20:08.150 --> 00:20:12.100
You could say he's a doggy, but maybe specifically
a Cavalier Spaniel? Or maybe a Chihuahua?

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.190
Yui-chan?

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:18.020
If he displays the same perfect conduct
he did in the group competition,

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:21.240
he may come across
a bit empty in the individuals.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:55.070
Kaji-kun sounds fiercer than usual.

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:57.640
Could this be... a new Kaji-kun?!

00:20:57.640 --> 00:21:00.940
That's it! A new Kaji-kun has been born!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:03.870
<i>Sensei, I understand now.</i>

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:06.430
<i>After hearing Arakawa's
hearty, daring sound...</i>

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:10.370
<i>I can't let this chance to take on
Tanuma Souichi pass me by!</i>

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.040
<i>This is completely different
from his group performance.</i>

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:22.060
<i>Back then, it was like a flowing wind.</i>

00:21:22.060 --> 00:21:23.000
<i>But now...</i>

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:28.700
<i>It's a fierce gale blowing
down from the peaks.</i>

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.860
<i>A wind from the mountains.</i>

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:38.620
It's a little sloppy, though.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.120
It's fierce, but just like in
the group competition,

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:58.550
his posture is beautiful and his
fingering isn't even the slightest bit off.

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:03.470
<i>This is like a good kid
trying to be rebellious.</i>

00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:08.130
<i>This is hard.</i>

00:22:08.600 --> 00:22:11.850
<i>My arms are screaming.
They feel like they're going to cramp up!</i>

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:14.610
<i>There's slack in one of the strings.</i>
